// ContextMod Devvit — example: auto-approve posts from trusted contributors.
//
// Demonstrates:
//   - Top-level `namedRules` map (camelCase, NOT `named_rules`).
//   - Reference via `{kind: 'named', name: '...'}` from a check's rules array
//     (NOT `{kind: 'ruleSet', name: '...'}` — that would be a `ruleset` rule
//     which is for inline AND/OR composition, NOT a named-rule reference).
//   - `combinator: 'OR'` so EITHER trusted-mod OR verified-old-account passes.
//   - `postBehavior: 'stop'` to halt the run after this check fires
//     (skip remaining checks for this thing).
//
// Reference: ../README.md "Config schema" + src/schema/app.schema.json.
//
// Schema notes (vs older example drift):
//   - `criteria` → `filter` on author rules.
//   - `condition` → `combinator` on checks.
//   - `named_rules` → `namedRules`.
//   - `{kind: 'ruleSet', name: 'X'}` (reference attempt) → `{kind: 'named', name: 'X'}`.
//   - `postBehavior: 'continue'` is NOT valid — default behavior is 'next'.
{
  namedRules: {
    'trusted-mod-or-contributor': {
      kind: 'author',
      filter: {
        isMod: true,
      },
    },
    'verified-old-account': {
      kind: 'author',
      filter: {
        verified: true,
        ageMinSec: 31536000,       // older than 365 days
        linkKarmaMin: 2500,
        commentKarmaMin: 2500,
      },
    },
  },
  runs: [
    {
      name: 'fast-track-trusted',
      checks: [
        {
          name: 'approve-on-trusted-author',
          // OR: EITHER trusted-mod-or-contributor OR verified-old-account passes.
          combinator: 'OR',
          rules: [
            { kind: 'named', name: 'trusted-mod-or-contributor' },
            { kind: 'named', name: 'verified-old-account' },
          ],
          actions: [
            { kind: 'approve' },
          ],
          // Halt the run after this check fires — skip remaining checks for
          // this thing. Valid values: 'next' (default), 'stop', or
          // `{goto: '<check-name>'}` (jump within the same run).
          postBehavior: 'stop',
        },
      ],
    },
  ],
}
